% ============================================================================
% possessive-noun.query.adj — a worked recall over the possessive-noun
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what kind of
% possessive noun is this?": it states no fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine
% resolves each `?` against the `possessive_noun` rows and returns the
% category + the table's own source/locator/trust. A noun the table does
% not carry abstains honestly — the engine never invents a classification.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli possessive-noun.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "possessive-noun.adj"

? possessive_noun(dog, $Category)        % expect singular_possessive
? possessive_noun($Word, plural_possessive) % expect bottles
? possessive_noun(cat, $Category)        % expect abstain -- no example sentence is shipped for this noun
